#: ../../BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.rst:5
msgid "二重井戸ポテンシャル Part 1"
msgstr "Double-Well Potential, Part 1"

#: ../../BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.rst:7
msgid ""
"立方晶 BaTiO₃ の Ti だけを中心からずらすと、どこでエネルギーが最も低くなるでしょうか。\\ OpenMX の計算では中心を挟む 2 "
"か所に極小が現れ、格子定数を 5% 大きくすると井戸が深くなりました。\\ 基準の格子定数 :math:`a_0` では、SevenNet（モデル"
" ``7net-mf-ompa``）と FairChem は中心付近の曲線の形を定性的に再現し、CHGNet "
"では変位に伴うエネルギー低下は小さくなりました。"
msgstr ""
"Where is the energy lowest when only Ti is displaced from the center in "
"cubic BaTiO₃? \\  The OpenMX calculations yielded two minima on either "
"side of the center, and increasing the lattice constant by 5% deepened "
"the wells. \\  At the reference lattice constant :math:`a_0`, SevenNet "
"(model ``7net-mf-ompa``) and FairChem qualitatively reproduced the shape "
"of the curve near the center, whereas CHGNet gave a smaller decrease in "
"energy upon displacement."

#: ../../BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.rst:11
msgid ""
"格子定数を :math:`1.05a_0` にすると、SevenNet と FairChem の井戸は OpenMX より約 35～37% "
"深く、変位ゼロを基準とした最小エネルギーは CHGNet（−102.69 meV/f.u.）が OpenMX（−101.26 "
"meV/f.u.）に最も近くなりました。"
msgstr ""
"At a lattice constant of :math:`1.05a_0`, the wells from SevenNet and "
"FairChem were about 35–37% deeper than the OpenMX wells. For the minimum "
"energy relative to zero displacement, CHGNet (−102.69 meV/f.u.) gave the "
"closest value to OpenMX (−101.26 meV/f.u.)."

#: ../../BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.rst:14
msgid "計算の動機"
msgstr "Motivation for the Calculations"

#: ../../BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.rst:16
msgid ""
"Sehrawat らの方法 :sup:`[1]` に従い、Ti だけを :math:`[001]` 方向にずらし、Ba と O "
"を理想立方晶の位置に固定します。\\ 変位ごとに構造を固定したまま全エネルギーを計算し、DFT と複数の\\ `機械学習原子間ポテンシャル "
"<https://technical-notes.quemix.com/md/mlip.html>`__\\ （MLIP）で比較します。\\ "
"中心の両側に等価な極小が現れる曲線を\\ `二重井戸ポテンシャル <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/soft_mode.html#double-well-potential>`__\\ "
"と呼びます。\\ この形は、Ti が中心からずれるとエネルギーが下がることを示します。"
msgstr ""
"Following the method of Sehrawat et al. :sup:`[1]`, we displace only Ti "
"along :math:`[001]` and fix Ba and O at their ideal cubic positions. \\  "
"At each displacement, we keep the structure fixed and calculate the total"
" energy using DFT and several \\  `machine-learning interatomic "
"potentials <https://technical-notes.quemix.com/md/mlip.html>`__ \\  "
"(MLIPs) for comparison. \\  A curve with equivalent minima on both sides "
"of the center is called a \\  `double-well potential <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/soft_mode.html#double-well-potential>`__\\ . \\  "
"This shape shows that displacing Ti from the center lowers the energy."

#: ../../BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.rst:21
msgid ""
"高温の常誘電相でも、平均構造が立方晶のまま、瞬間的には Ti が中心からずれて局所的な極性を持ち得ます（技術ノートの\\ "
"`局所的なTiの変位と平均構造 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html#fe-local-average>`__）。\\ "
"ここで計算する静的エネルギー曲線は、Ti の変位だけを取り出した断面です。\\ 原子の協同変位は :doc:`Part 2 <total-"
"energy>`、有限温度での局所変位は :doc:`構造相転移 <phase_transition>` で扱います。"
msgstr ""
"Even in the high-temperature paraelectric phase, the average structure "
"can remain cubic while instantaneous off-center Ti displacements give "
"rise to local polarity (see \\  `local Ti displacements and average "
"structure <https://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html"
"#fe-local-average>`__ in the Technical Notes). \\  The static energy "
"curve calculated here is a slice through the energy surface along the Ti "
"displacement coordinate alone. \\  Cooperative displacements are covered "
"in :doc:`Part 2 <total-energy>`, and local displacements at finite "
"temperature are covered in :doc:`Structural Phase Transitions "
"<phase_transition>`."

#: ../../BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.rst:28
msgid "入力ファイル例"
msgstr "Example Input Files"

#: ../../BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.rst:30
msgid ""
"以下は、立方晶 BaTiO₃ の Ti 原子を [001] 方向へ ``+0.08 Å`` 変位させ、\\ "
"各構造の全エネルギーを評価するための入力ファイル例です。\\ この入力例を基準として Ti "
"変位量を正負方向に変更し、各変位点で単点エネルギーを計算することで、\\ 二重井戸ポテンシャルの曲線を作成できます。"
msgstr ""
"These example input files displace Ti in cubic BaTiO₃ along [001] by "
"``+0.08 Å`` from its ideal position \\  and evaluate the total energy of "
"each structure. \\  Using these files as templates, you can vary the Ti "
"displacement in both directions \\  and calculate the single-point energy"
" at each displacement to obtain the double-well potential curve."

#: ../../BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.rst:35
msgid ""
"本計算では、Ba 原子および O 原子を理想立方晶位置に固定し、**Ti 原子の z 座標だけを変更します**。\\ "
"構造最適化やセル緩和を行うと指定した変位座標が変化するため、各変位で\\ `単点計算 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html#structure-"
"optimization>`__\\ を行います。\\ OpenMX では ``MD.Type Nomd``、CHGNet では ``run "
"0`` を用います。SevenNet では、計算条件を ``ase.in`` に記述し、\\ 実際の Ti 変位は ``rsdft.atoms``"
" の分率座標で指定します。"
msgstr ""
"We keep Ba and O at their ideal cubic positions and **change only the z "
"coordinate of Ti**. \\  Geometry optimization or cell relaxation would "
"change the specified displacement, so we run a \\  `single-point "
"calculation <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html#structure-"
"optimization>`__ \\  at each displacement. \\  We use ``MD.Type Nomd`` in"
" OpenMX and ``run 0`` in CHGNet. For SevenNet, we set the calculation "
"conditions in ``ase.in``, \\  and specify the Ti displacement using "
"fractional coordinates in ``rsdft.atoms``."

